[{"id":4407675853,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBrfLzQ","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","commit_id":"f8d76f36797b014bc8b69a936900246ea2bc0fa9","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?u=b7882c94f408976a2f79e8fe6e1ce27fbd48db74&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","login":"HolonProduction","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction"},"body":"The approach taken here does not work for a dynamic call:\n\n```gdscript\n@abstract class T extends RefCounted:\n\tpass\n\nvar a: Variant = T\n\nfunc _run() -> void:\n    print(a.can_instantiate())\n    print(a.new())\n```\n\nThis still produces an object (although not an instance of the script). `CALL_ERROR_INVALID_METHOD` falls back to calling on the native class which creates a `RefCounted` instance in this case.\n\nI'm also not sure about this returning an error method thing. This works when using the methodbind from the GDScriptVM. But couldn't it mess up extensions?","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119932#pullrequestreview-4407675853","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119932","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-06-02T07:55:29Z"},{"id":4408285587,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBsEZkw","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"d8f82123ce83b9f07b4aa4fa4ff3b9deb381a96b","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?u=b7882c94f408976a2f79e8fe6e1ce27fbd48db74&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","login":"HolonProduction","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119932#pullrequestreview-4408285587","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119932","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-06-02T09:16:01Z"},{"id":4408437668,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBsNrpA","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"d8f82123ce83b9f07b4aa4fa4ff3b9deb381a96b","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?u=0565b5d99d54afd5fda6712cd8eb05893572baed&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","login":"dalexeev","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119932#pullrequestreview-4408437668","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119932","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-06-02T09:37:13Z"},{"id":4491158214,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABC7Gixg","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"a7ef3cc3b8df0239daa095816b6aabee56431631","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?u=b7882c94f408976a2f79e8fe6e1ce27fbd48db74&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","login":"HolonProduction","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction"},"body":"Makes sense to me.\n\nThe usage of `CALL_ERROR_INVALID_METHOD` for a valid method bind, might trigger some edge case. But since no-one from core did raise concerns, I guess we can just try it.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119932#pullrequestreview-4491158214","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119932","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-06-13T08:31:15Z"},{"id":4677937147,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFtOn-w","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"a7ef3cc3b8df0239daa095816b6aabee56431631","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","login":"Ivorforce","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce"},"body":"Have only reviewed the code at a glance so I can't approve.\n\nHowever, regarding `CALL_ERROR_INVALID_METHOD`: I don't think there should be a problem with using that.\nThe enum case is already used in various different ways, so this should not add significant new complexity.\nOn a theoretical level, maybe rejecting a call to an abstract constructor should throw a kind of \"protected function call\" error — clearly the method is valid if a subclass can call it. But we don't really have a use case for introducing a new case.\n\nOverall, let's merge it.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119932#pullrequestreview-4677937147","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119932","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-07-11T13:51:01Z"}]